## ROOT CAUSE

**D1** — verifier #40 replaced the gerund arm's verb whitelist with a "structural" test that has two escapes a proper-name object defeats simultaneously: guard A is a **closed finite-verb list** (throws, fails, triggers, revokes, generates, reorders, queues, resets, consumes, starts, gives, returns, stops are not on it); guard B is `^<Gerund>\s+(?:an?\b|(?:[a-z]+\s+){0,2}[a-z]+s\b)`, which **can only fire when the object is lowercase**. #40 closed the generic-object half of #39's class and left the proper-name half — the form a Brain OS answer actually takes — fully open. **Fourth recurrence of this arm.**

**D2** — two compounding: (1) **inverted polarity** — the X-guard's stoplist lists `no|nothing|none` inside a *negative* lookahead, so those are precisely the words that do **not** get its protection; (2) the arm's negation check runs on text up to the **end of the matched participle** (run19/D134), so an object negator is outside the checked span **by construction**.

